:: Spa Members Party First Round
<<endevent>><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>><<famesocial 5>>
You take a drink that tastes of lime, mint, and flowers, then move towards a small group near a low table. They talk like old friends, but every sentence carries money. Villas. Import permits. A charity dinner where the seating plan matters more than the charity itself.
<br><br>
<<set _partyLine to random(1, 6)>>
<<if _partyLine is 1>>
	A <<person>> asks which family brought you here. When you say none, <<he>> laughs into <<his>> glass. "Even better. People love a self-made story."
<<elseif _partyLine is 2>>
	"I thought you were someone's guest," a <<person>> says. <<He>> looks again. "No. You're here by yourself. That is much rarer."
<<elseif _partyLine is 3>>
	Two guests lower their voices as you pass. You catch the words "HBSC" and "at that age", followed by a look that is almost respectful.
<<elseif _partyLine is 4>>
	A <<person>> praises the way you hold yourself, then your looks, then pretends <<he>> only meant the first part.
<<elseif _partyLine is 5>>
	Someone asks what you think about a charity dinner, then listens as if your answer might change the guest list.
<<else>>
	An older guest smiles over the rim of <<his>> drink. "Be careful. Rooms like this make you feel welcome until you forget they bite."
<</if>>
<br><br>
You learn quickly that the trick is not to talk too much. The rich leave silences in conversation and wait to see who rushes to fill them. You let a few silences pass. That earns you more interest than bragging would have.
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Follow the conversation to the terrace (0:25)|Spa Members Party Terrace]]>><<pass 25>><<stress -3>><</link>><<lstress>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Spa]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Spa Members Party Terrace
<<endevent>><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>><<famesocial 5>>
The terrace is warmer than the lounge. Night air carries the smell of flowers, chlorine, and expensive perfume. Guests sit around a low fire pit with bare ankles, open collars, and easy laughter that still feels practised.
<br><br>
A <<person>> waves you into the circle. "We were deciding whether ambition is rude. You arrived at the right time."
<br><br>
<<set _blendLine to random(1, 5)>>
<<if _blendLine is 1>>
	You say ambition is only rude when it fails. The table goes quiet, then someone laughs hard enough to spill a drink.
<<elseif _blendLine is 2>>
	You say people born rich like to call hunger ugly. A guest in pearls raises their brows, but does not argue.
<<elseif _blendLine is 3>>
	You shrug and say you have been called worse. That wins a few smiles, and one guest starts watching you like a possible investment.
<<elseif _blendLine is 4>>
	You turn the question back on them. They enjoy that. Rich people like being studied, as long as it makes them feel important.
<<else>>
	You let the silence sit for a moment, then ask what makes ambition respectable. The circle spends the next five minutes arguing with itself.
<</if>>
<br><br>
The party loosens around you. Someone orders another round. Someone asks where you buy your clothes, then tries not to look disappointed when your answer gives them nothing useful.
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Let them study you properly (0:20)|Spa Members Party Beauty Talk]]>><<pass 20>><<stress -4>><</link>><<lstress>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Spa]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Spa Members Party Beauty Talk
<<endevent>><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>><<famesocial 5>>
<<if $beautyBoost and $beautyBoost.spa and $beautyBoost.spa.amount > 0 and getSpaBeautyBoost() > 0>>
	<<if random(1, 6) is 1>>
		A <<person>> studies you with envy. "You had the <<print $beautyBoost.spa.treatment>>, didn't you? That finish is hard to fake. Good choice. Annoyingly good."
	<<elseif random(1, 6) is 2>>
		"Your skin catches the lantern light," a <<person>> says. <<He>> leans closer, then smiles. "Sorry. That sounded less strange in my head."
	<<elseif random(1, 6) is 3>>
		A guest taps <<his>> cheek, thinking. "The spa has improved. Last season everyone came out looking shiny. You look rested. Much better. Much more dangerous."
	<<elseif random(1, 6) is 4>>
		"That treatment suits you," a <<person>> says. "Some people pay to look rich and only manage to look scared. You still look like yourself."
	<<elseif random(1, 6) is 5>>
		Someone asks whether the effect is difficult to keep. Before you can answer, another guest says, "Of course it is. Beauty that lasts always sends a bill later."
	<<else>>
		A <<person>> smiles over <<his>> drink. "Whatever they did downstairs, keep doing it. People are trying not to stare, which means they are staring all the time."
	<</if>>
<<else>>
	<<if random(1, 3) is 1>>
		A <<person>> asks whether you have booked a treatment yet. "You should. Half the people here buy an hour of peace and call it maintenance."
	<<elseif random(1, 3) is 2>>
		Someone recommends the caviar suite, then admits <<he>> mostly likes the name. "White caviar immersion. It sounds like a threat from a very rich fish."
	<<else>>
		"The diamond programme is obscene," a <<person>> says. "That does not mean it is bad. Some obscene things are excellent."
	<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
The comments should feel shallow, but they do not. In this room, appearance is a language. Everyone here can read money, effort, fear, and confidence with a single glance.
<br><br>
<<socialiseicon>><<link [[Stay for one more round (0:30)|Spa Members Party Final Round]]>><<pass 30>><<stress -4>><</link>><<lstress>>
<br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Spa]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Spa Members Party Final Round
<<endevent>><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>><<famesocial 5>>
Later, the music grows softer and the party spreads out. Some guests move towards the steam rooms. Others stay by the pool with their shoes under their chairs, talking about investments, lovers, scandals, and wellness in the same light voice.
<br><br>
A <<person>> sits beside you, close enough to speak quietly without making it intimate.
<<set _finalLine to random(1, 5)>>
<<if _finalLine is 1>>
	<<He>> points out three guests who will pretend not to remember you tomorrow, and two who certainly will.
<<elseif _finalLine is 2>>
	<<He>> warns you that every compliment here is also a test. "But a test is not always an attack. Sometimes it is how they decide whether to make space."
<<elseif _finalLine is 3>>
	"Most people either apologise for being here or try too hard. You are doing neither. That will annoy people."
<<elseif _finalLine is 4>>
	<<He>> laughs when someone across the terrace raises a glass to you. "There. Now you are a small mystery. Use that before they solve you."
<<else>>
	<<He>> says nothing for a while, then gives you the name of a tailor, a quiet accountant, and a hotel bar where half the town agrees on its respectable lies.
<</if>>
<br><br>
You blend with the rich well enough to worry them.<<lstress>><<stress -6>>
<br><br>
<<if $money >= (setup.inflation ? setup.inflation.price(225000) : 225000)>>
	<<spaicon "massage">><<link [[Call your personal masseur before leaving (1:30)|Spa Private Masseur]]>><<money -225000 "spa">><<pass 90>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Return to the foyer|Spa]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Spa Members Party X-Change Gossip
<<endevent>><<effects>><<set $outside to 0>><<generate1>><<person1>><<famesocial 15>>
A small group is already seated together: an older <<person>> with silver rings on every finger, a younger couple who keep finishing each other's sentences, and a <<generate2>><<person2>><<person>> in a linen suit who has not spoken yet. The one in linen watches the room with the careful attention of someone who has learned when not to talk.
<br><br>
The <<person1>><<person>> with the rings gestures for you to sit. "A new face. You look like someone who still believes this town runs on hard work and good weather."
<br><br>
A few of the others laugh softly. Not at you. At the idea.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Spa Party Gossip Pills]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Spa Party Gossip Pills
<<effects>>
"Have you ever wondered," the <<person1>><<person>> with the rings says, swirling <<his>> drink, "why this town is so... like this?"
<br><br>
<<person2>>The <<person>> in the linen suit shifts. "That is not a party conversation."
<br><br>
"Anything can be party talk, if you want it to be." <<person1>>The <<person>> with the rings leans back. "The pills. You know about the pills? Everyone in this room does. The ones that change your body, confuse your sense of self, and make you forget what you were angry about because you are too busy dealing with a new body."
<br><br>
The younger couple exchange a glance. And one of them says, "They are recreational. People take them at parties."
<br><br>
"People take them because they are <i>available</i>," <<person1>>the <<person>> corrects. "Have you ever asked yourself why something that powerful, that dangerous, is easier to find in this town than a decent plumber?"
<br><br>
<<link [[Keep listening|Spa Party Gossip Control]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask who supplies them|Spa Party Gossip Bank]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>
<br><br>
<<getouticon>><<link [[Excuse yourself|Spa Members Party]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>

:: Spa Party Gossip Control
<<effects>>
<<person1>>The <<person>> with the rings lowers <<his>> voice, though no one outside the circle could hear over the music. "Think about what the pills actually do. Not the party trick. The result. Someone takes one, their body changes, their hormones shift, and their sense of identity breaks in two. What happens to a person in that state?"
<br><br>
<<He>> counts on <<his>> fingers. "They become confused. Vulnerable. Dependent on whoever can explain what is happening to them. They stop paying attention to their jobs, their relationships, and the town around them. They become... <i>easy to govern</i>."
<br><br>
<<person2>>The <<person>> in the linen suit sets <<his>> glass down. "You are describing a conspiracy."
<br><br>
"I am describing an economy." <<person1>><<He>> smiles without warmth. "Confused people do not organise. People chasing pleasure do not protest. People made chemically stupid, and I am sorry, but that is what I mean, do not ask why the rents keep climbing while the wages do not."
<br><br>
The younger man speaks for the first time. "You make it sound deliberate."
<br><br>
"Because it is. It is the cheapest form of control ever invented. Cheaper than police. Cheaper than propaganda. You just make the pills available and let human nature do the rest," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask about the mayor|Spa Party Gossip Quinn]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Spa Party Gossip Bank
<<effects>>
"No one knows for certain, but follow the money," <<person1>>the <<person>> with the rings says. <<He>> taps the arm of the sofa for emphasis. "Who in this town has the money to fund a supply network that large? Who has the connections to make sure it is never investigated, never seized, and never even mentioned in the local press?"
<br><br>
<<He>> pauses. Waits. Lets the silence do the work.
<br><br>
<<person2>>"The bank," the <<person>> in the linen suit says quietly, as though admitting something <<he>> has known for a long time and hoped was not true.
<br><br>
<<person1>>"The bank," <<he>> confirms. "HBSC. Or more precisely, the person who runs it. Not the board. They are accountants and yes-men. The <span class="elk">owner</span>. The one whose name you will not find on the official papers, but whose signature is on every decision that matters."
<br><br>
The younger guest frowns. "That is a serious accusation."
<br><br>
"It is a serious town." <<person1>><<He>> finishes <<his>> drink. "Where do you think the funding comes from? The pills are not made in a garage. There are labs, transport routes, and distribution networks. That takes money. Real money. The kind that only comes from an institution no one is allowed to audit."
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask about the mayor|Spa Party Gossip Quinn]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Spa Party Gossip Quinn
<<effects>>
The younger one voices what you were thinking. "What about the mayor? Quinn. <<nnpc_He 'Quinn'>> must know."
<br><br>
<<person1>>The <<person>> with the rings laughs without humour. "Know? <<nnpc_He 'Quinn'>> allows it. Why do you think the bank is still standing? Why do you think no regulator has ever knocked on HBSC's door? A bank that size, in a town this small, with that kind of influence... you do not survive without political cover."
<br><br>
"Quinn is not stupid," <<he>> continues. "<<nnpc_He 'Quinn'>> is practical. <<nnpc_He 'Quinn'>> looks at the numbers and decides that whatever is happening under the surface is a price <<nnpc_he 'Quinn'>> is willing to let someone else pay. That is policy."
<br><br>
<<person2>>The <<person>> in the linen suit pinches the bridge of <<his>> nose. "You are saying the mayor and the bank are—"
<br><br>
<<person1>>"They feed each other." <<He>> reaches for a fresh glass from a passing tray. "The bank provides stability. The mayor provides cover. The pills provide control. Everyone in this room benefits from the arrangement, which is why no one in this room will ever do anything about it."
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask what else they know|Spa Party Gossip Cult]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Spa Party Gossip Cult
<<effects>>
<<person2>>The <<person>> in the linen suit has been quiet for a while. Now <<he>> leans forward, elbows on <<his>> knees, and speaks in a voice so low you have to lean in to catch it.
<br><br>
"There is something else," <<he>> says. "Something I have only heard once, and from someone who was drunk enough to regret saying it the next morning."
<br><br>
<<person1>>The <<person>> with the rings raises an eyebrow but does not interrupt.
<br><br>
<<person2>>"The bank owner does not work alone. There is a circle. A group. Some call it a society, some a council, but the word I heard was cult." <<He>> pauses. "Old money. Old names. People who were powerful in this place before there was a town. They do not meet in boardrooms. They meet in places that are not on any map."
<br><br>
"That is a rumour," the younger guest says.
<br><br>
"So were the pills, once. I do not know what they believe. I do not know what they do behind closed doors. But I know one thing." <<He>> glances around the room as though checking for faces he does not recognise. "Their symbol. The person who told me drew it on a napkin before tearing it up."
<br><br>
"What was it?"
<br><br>
<<person2>>"An elk," <<he>> says. "Antlers and all."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Spa Party Gossip End]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Spa Party Gossip End
<<effects>>
The conversation breaks apart after that. Someone refills their glass. The younger couple leave without saying goodbye. 
<br><br>
<<person1>>The <<person>> with the rings watches them go, then turns to you. "You are very quiet. That is either wisdom or shock. Either way, it is the correct response."
<br><br>
<<He>> stands, brushing invisible dust from <<his>> sleeve. "Enjoy the party. And if you ever see an elk in a place where there should not be one, do yourself a favour. <i>Do not ask about it</i>."
<br><br>
<<He>> walks away. The music swells to fill the silence <<he>> leaves behind.
<br><br>
You sit alone on the sofa for a moment. The room is the same, with crystal glasses, linen, and laughter, but it feels different now.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Spa Party Gossip End 2]]>><<pass 5>><</link>>

:: Spa Party Gossip End 2
<<effects>><<set $daily.spaXChangeGossip to true>>
As you stand to leave, your eye catches something on the far wall, half-hidden behind a decorative screen. A piece of art you had not noticed before: a watercolour of a forest clearing, painted in muted greens and golds. It is unremarkable, the sort of thing you would walk past a hundred times without looking.
<br><br>
But in the centre of the clearing, barely visible between the trees, stands a figure with branching antlers.
<br><br>
You blink. Look again. It is just a painting of trees.<<stress 4>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
<<if $awareness lt 500>>
	<span class="lblue">You feel more aware of the forces shaping this place.</span><<awareness 5>><<gawareness>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Return to the party|Spa Members Party]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
